      "title": "Tenured Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Tenured Associate/Full Professor Johns Hopkins University: Zanvyl Krieger School of Arts and Sciences: Department of Biophysics Location Baltimore, MD, 21218 Open Date Sep 14, 2026 Salary Range or Pay Grade Associate Professor: $135,500-207,000 | Professor: $161,000-325,500 Description The Thomas C. Jenkins Department of Biophysics ( https://biophysics.jhu.edu/ ) invites applications for tenure d appointments at the Associate and Full Professor ranks in the area of theoretical or computational biophysics. Applicants should demonstrate their capacity for innovative and rigorous application of computational and theoretical approaches to problems in molecular or cellular biology or related topics. Successful applicants will join a vibrant and collaborative biophysics community at Johns Hopkins which includes the T.C. Jenkins Department of Biophysics in Arts & Sciences and the Department of Biophysics and Biophysical Chemistry at the School of Medicine. We are aiming for multiple hires in this search. Qualifications A Ph.D. and postdoctoral experience or equivalent are required. Application Instructions Please submit the following materials: Curriculum Vitae (CV) Research statement Statement of teaching interests and philosophy Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis beginning October 20, 2026. Additional Instructions: Research Statement Should cover past and planned research. Maximum 5 pages, including figures but not including references. We encourage at most 2 pages of past work. Describe your most significant scientific accomplishments to date and explain why they are significant. Describe your goals and vision for your future research program in the Johns Hopkins biophysics environment. Include relevant details that articulate how you will achieve these goals. Describe experiences and qualifications that have positioned you to achieve those goals, and how pursuit of your goals will advance the frontier of knowledge. Curriculum Vitae Include your educational and training history; significant activities in research, education, and diversity service; honors and awards; presentations; and published and accepted papers. Preprints or papers under review will be considered if they have been deposited on BioRxiv or similar public preprint server. Teaching Statement Maximum 2 pages. Describe your approach to undergraduate and graduate teaching, and the subjects you would most like to teach. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Salary Range The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on Johns Hopkins University's good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's geographic location, skills, work experience, internal equity, market conditions, education/training and other factors, as reasonably determined by the University. Total Rewards Johns Hopkins offers a total rewards package that supports our employees' health, life, career and retirement. More information can be found here: https://hr.jhu.edu/benefits-worklife/ . Equal Opportunity Employer The Johns Hopkins University is committed to equal opportunity for its faculty, staff, and students. To that end, the university does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, marital status, pregnancy, race, color, ethnicity, national origin, age, disability, religion, sexual 