    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193449": {
      "title": "Apply",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In GU Radiation Oncologist Johns Hopkins University: School of Medicine: Department of Radiation Oncology and Molecular Radiation Sciences Location Baltimore, MD, 21224 Open Date Sep 11, 2026 Salary Range or Pay Grade 200,000 - 400,000 Description The Johns Hopkins Department of Radiation Oncology and Molecular Radiation Sciences is seeking an outstanding academically-focused radiation oncologist with a focus in genitourinary cancer to join the Department at our Johns Hopkins Hospital location.  Clinical activities will include multi-disciplinary clinic participation and collaborations with GU medical oncologists and urologists.  Participation within the Sidney Kimmel Comprehensive Cancer Center will be encouraged.  Research can combine clinical, physics and/or biology-based interests, with an emphasis on innovative clinical trials.   The successful candidate will work closely with the clinical team at Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine, the Johns Hopkins Hospital, Bayview Hospital and the National Capital Region.  Requirements include a M.D. degree(s), ABR board certification or eligibility, demonstrated clinical competency in Radiation Oncology and a strong interest in the clinical care and research.  Salary will be commensurate with experience and qualifications.  Letter of interest and CV should be sent via e-mail to rwhite60@jhmi.edu or by mail to: Akila N. Viswanathan, MD MPH Professor and Chair Department of Radiation Oncology and Molecular Radiation Sciences Johns Hopkins Medicine – Weinberg Building – Suite 14490 401 N. Broadway – Baltimore, MD  21287 Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free