    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192385": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sociology",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Assistant Professor of Sociology – Baltimore, MD Johns Hopkins University: Zanvyl Krieger School of Arts and Sciences: Department of Sociology Location Baltimore, MD, 21218 Open Date Sep 02, 2026 Salary Range or Pay Grade $102,500 to $144,500/year Deadline Oct 01, 2026 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description The Johns Hopkins Department of Sociology seeks a sociologist of outstanding international reputation or promise for a tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Sociology. This position requires a PhD in Sociology. Priority will be given to a candidate with strong quantitative and computational skills and research focus on historical sociology and/or theory. Job duties will include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in sociology, conducting empirical research in high-impact fields of sociology, and advising undergraduate and graduate students. DUTIES: Teach courses in the Krieger School of Arts and Sciences, the Department of Sociology Qualifications REQUIREMENTS: Ph.D. in Sociology or related field. Successful candidates will have a record of excellent empirical research in any field(s) of sociology and will join a growing, vibrant Department of Sociology within a School and University that foster a wide range of interdisciplinary conversations and collaborations. Applicants should have a record of published scholarship in sociology. Application Instructions Applications should include a current CV and cover letter. Do not include references or letters of recommendation; if needed, candidates may be contacted later for further information. Applications must be received by Friday, September 25th, 2026. Any questions about the search process should be directed to sociology@jhu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Do