    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192520": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Postdoctoral Fellow - Applied Mathematics & Statistics Johns Hopkins University: Whiting School of Engineering: Department of Applied Mathematics & Statistics Location Baltimore, MD, 21218 Open Date Aug 28, 2026 Salary Range or Pay Grade $63,840 - $100,000+ Description The Johns Hopkins University’s Department of Applied Mathematics and Statistics invites applicants for the position of Postdoctoral Fellow in the lab of Professor Shiqian Ma. Candidates must have completed their Ph.D. prior to their appointment start date, and no later than 01/01/2027 and show definite promise in research and teaching. This position may include a teaching load of one course per year, depending on funding and needs of the department, so that the appointee will have ample time for research. The appointment is for one year, with possibility of renewal, depending on funding availability. The successful candidate will be expected to collaborate with Professor Shiqian Ma on mathematical foundations and optimization of modern machine learning and AI. Particular interests include the theory and design of adaptive algorithms, methods, exploiting geometric structures in optimization, and optimization algorithms motivated by the training of large-scale machine learning models. A strong background and demonstrated research experience in machine learning and optimization are required. Applicants are asked to submit (a) an AMS standard coversheet; (b) a curriculum vitae; (c) a description of research interests and have at least three letters of recommendation submitted. Applicants should apply using: https://apply.interfolio.com/192520 Applications received by 09/20/2026 will be guaranteed full consideration; early application is advisable. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receiv