    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192477": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Lecturer Johns Hopkins University: Zanvyl Krieger School of Arts and Sciences: Department of Psychological & Brain Sciences Location Baltimore, MD, 21218 Open Date Aug 27, 2026 Salary Range or Pay Grade $10,000 Description Position Overview Adjunct Faculty, Behavioral Biology Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences Zanvyl Krieger School of Arts and Sciences Johns Hopkins University General Description The Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences ( http://pbs.jhu.edu/ ) at Johns Hopkins University invites applications for a non-tenure track adjunct faculty member within the David S. Olton Behavioral Biology Program to teach Animal Behavior. We are especially interested in candidates with a passion for teaching and a strong record in the classroom, delivering high-quality education to undergraduate students. Animal Behavior – 200.208 This course examines how and why animal behaviors are produced across the animal kingdom. Neurobiological, hormonal and developmental mechanisms and adaptive function of behaviors are examined in an evolutionary context. Behaviors include survival, acquiring food, reproduction, communication, parental care, and cooperation. Students will also learn how to develop hypotheses and predictions for scientific questions and interpret graphical results. Qualifications A Ph.D. (or ABD) in psychology, biology, neuroscience, ethology, or a related discipline, a master’s degree at minimum. Teaching experience is essential. Application Instructions Candidates should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, relevant teaching evaluations, and the names of at least three references. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            c