      "title": "Baltimore GIM Clinician Scientist",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Baltimore GIM Clinician Scientist Johns Hopkins University: School of Medicine Location Baltimore, MD, 21287 Open Date May 19, 2026 Salary Range or Pay Grade $85,933 - $136,228 Description This position is a dedicated Researcher who can work remotely. The faculty member will be a researcher who will work on other PI’s research for the Division of General Internal Medicine. Research Structure · Will either work on own grant or other PI grants Clinical Structure None Salary Structure The referenced salary range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. Additional compensation may be earned through incentive programs and call supplements. There is a quarterly RVU bonus, details provided during the interview phase. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary range stated herein. For more information, please contact the hiring department. Program Highlights High-volume, nationally ranked academic program Extensive collaboration across Johns Hopkins schools and departments Strong institutional support for academic development and mentorship Opportunities for leadership, education, and scholarly activity Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Salary Range The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on Johns Hopkins University's good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. The actual compensation offered to the selected candidate may vary and will ulti