      "title": "Apply",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Breast Radiation Oncologist Johns Hopkins University: School of Medicine: Department of Radiation Oncology and Molecular Radiation Sciences Location Bethesda, MD, 20814 Open Date Mar 30, 2026 Salary Range or Pay Grade $200,000 - $400,000 per year Description The Johns Hopkins Department of Radiation Oncology and Molecular Radiation Sciences is seeking a clinically focused radiation oncologist to join the Department at our Suburban Hospital location in Bethesda, Maryland.  Clinical activities will include multi-disciplinary clinic participation and collaborations with breast medical and surgical oncologists.  The primary focus will be on women’s health to include breast and gynecologic cancers, with appropriate selection of patients for photon, proton or brachytherapy treatment.  The successful candidate will work closely with the clinical team at Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine, Sibley Memorial Hospital, and The Johns Hopkins Hospital. Qualifications Requirements include a M.D. degree(s), ABR board certification or eligibility, demonstrated clinical competency in Radiation Oncology and a strong interest in the clinical care.  Salary will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Application Instructions Apply online with Letter of Interest and CV Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Salary Range The referenced salary range represents the minimum and maximum salaries for this position and is based on Johns Hopkins University's good faith belief at the time of posting. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end o